WEBVTT

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.420
So, it's going pretty well 
with your girlfriend?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.500
Yeah, it is. T-To tell the truth...

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.780
I'm thinking of proposing to her

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.290
once this business deal goes through.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.970
Well, that's a reason to celebrate.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
<b>If Her Flag Breaks{Kanojo ga flag wo oraretara}{Z: I just simplified colors here.}</b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.010
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.010
<b>I'm Going to Marry Her 
Once I Leave This School</b>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.010
<b>Hatagaya Academy High School</b>

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.140
<i>I don't get it...</i>

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.020
Students of Hatagaya Academy!

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.680
<i>What happened there?</i>

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.060
<i>I don't think it was 
just a normal accident.</i>

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.110
<i>I want to know.</i>

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.650
Stand.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:37.740
Bow.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.530
Take your seats.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.080
<i>And that kid...</i>

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.830
<i>He was wearing our uniform...</i>

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.960
<i>But Hatagaya Academy has classes from</i>

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.580
<i>kindergarten all the way to college.</i>

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.670
Okay, everyone.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.090
You're all going to

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.840
meet a new friend today.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.510
All right. Go ahead and come in.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.680
<i>I won't be able to 
find him that easi—</i>

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.980
<b>Hatate 
Souta</b>

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.400
My name is Hatate Souta.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.980
Nice to meet all of you.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.490
She stood up and then 
sat right back down...

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.660
Was she stretching?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.370
Why did she...

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.620
So where should we have 
our Souta-chan sit?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.290
"Chan"?!

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:31.460
Let's see...

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.130
Let's see...

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.670
How about...

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.340
There's an open seat right there.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.800
The seat right behind Nanami-chan.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.440
H-Hi there.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.320
<i>There's no doubt about it.</i>

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.940
<i>This is the same man.</i>

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.320
<i>That weird guy from this morning.</i>

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.450
Hey there, Hotate-kun.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.790
It's Hatate.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.790
Hatate-kun, nice to meet you.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.210
Nice to meet you, too.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.300
<i>Stare.</i>

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.380
Anyway, see you around.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.670
Hotate— I mean, Hatate.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.800
If you need something, just let me know.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.810
Also if you want to know about any 
of the girls, I've got your back.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.400
All the ladies like me, so I don't 
think I'll be needing your help.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.400
But no one likes me...

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.110
I'll let you be my servant. Be grateful.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.530
I'm sorry.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.820
I'm quite the sadist.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.830
Two sadists won't get along!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.790
Want to join us in our quest to become 
the number one high school baseball team?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.460
Sorry, I like soccer.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.920
Wait a second! Hotate Souta!

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.680
It's Hatate Souta.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.800
You shall give me a moment of your time.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.100
You see, I can't stand not solving 
any mystery that catches my eye.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.350
Now you shall tell me everything!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.310
Huh? T-Tell you what?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.900
Don't play dumb.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.570
I can see it glistening in front of me.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.650
Glistening?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:22.900
Like fresh fish or something?

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.570
You keep looking above people's heads—

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.240
right here—and then making some sort 
of decision based on that, aren't you?!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.950
Wh-What are you going on about?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.960
You looked again!

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.830
You can't fool my eyes!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.250
I can tell you keep worrying about

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.170
whatever's above my head!

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.800
That truck from this morning.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.510
I know you haven't forgotten.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.680
You were doing something strange.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.060
I know that's why all of that happened.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.770
I don't know what it was, 
but I'm certain you did something.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.690
You see something, don't you?!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.980
So you were at that intersection...

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.820
Yeah, I saw something.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:04.990
There was this fly—

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.240
Don't try to fool me with that rubbish!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.700
Now tell me what you did.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.580
Do you know about "flags"?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.370
Flags?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.080
I can actually see them.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.290
Y-You can see them?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.090
These flags, or whatever.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.720
Not just see them.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.720
I instinctively know what I have 
to do to destroy those flags,

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.470
as well.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.140
That's why I...

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.350
That business deal is 
never going to go through.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:40.440
I destroyed the "death flag" 
that was waving above his head.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.480
So did you do the same thing 
in the classroom, then?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.570
With that guy who was talking
about helping you with girls...

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.490
I shattered his "friendship flag."

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.910
And that girl who was coming on to you?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.240
That was her "romance flag."

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.090
That's funny.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.300
That's ridiculous.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.130
My stomach hurts.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.800
Give those bad gags of yours a rest.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.720
I understand the death flag,

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.720
but why destroy those 
friendship and romance flags?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.650
Are you trying to be a hero, who 
doesn't use his powers for his own good?

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.730
Everything you said was 
just a bad joke, correct?

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.650
I don't mind if you laugh at me.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.940
I didn't tell you because 
I wanted you to believe me.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.570
Misfortune comes to people 
who get too close to me.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.410
I don't want to

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.490
see people get hurt any longer.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.080
I need to be alone.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.000
<i>Alone...</i>

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.480
Anyway,

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.810
don't involve yourself with me anymore.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:04.150
It shouldn't matter 
to you if I'm a loner or not.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.150
Don't talk about being 
alone so trivially!

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:10.610
In the end, you're just rejecting 
anyone who approaches you.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.030
Have you heard about the 
Premium Ambriel disaster?

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.790
The luxury liner that sank 
the other day? What of it?

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.960
All of the passengers 
are missing, except one.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:25.090
Only a single person was rescued.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.540
<b>The truth behind the Premium Ambriel</b>

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.420
Hatate Souta: the lone survivor

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:26.960
That was me.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:28.670
What of it?!

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.760
I'm trying to tell you—

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:30.840
Enough of your double-talk!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.550
My eyes! My eyes!

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.930
I've had enough of those eyes of yours.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.930
What are you doing?!

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.810
I've had enough of your 
obsession with your own misfortune.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.270
I'm not trying to—

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.020
Most importantly,

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.060
I've had enough of you making me 
remember things I don't want to remember.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.230
Misfortune comes to people 
who get too close to you?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:47.980
Enough of your talk about being alone.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.230
How about taking a look?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.610
Is there a "flag" above my head, 
like the ones you've mentioned?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.570
How about it?!

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:54.950
N-No...

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:55.990
Indeed.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.080
Of course there isn't anything.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.120
I don't feel any love or friendship 
towards you in the slightest.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.870
And as such, I shouldn't have 
any of those flags of yours.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:04.580
Even I did, that 
overly self-defeating

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.960
attitude of yours would 
destroy it in an instant.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.630
If I don't like something about 
you, I'm going to tell you,

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.510
and when I want to yell 
at you, I'm going to yell.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.390
You should just do the same to me.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.640
In short...

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.470
Just stop looking so 
depressed in front of me...

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.480
You're a nice person.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.850
Thanks.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.450
Nanami Knight Bladefield.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:36.370
I hate being called by my 
last name. Use my first name.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.280
You add "-san" or "-chan," 
and you're dead.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.330
Right, Nanami.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.040
You can call me "Souta."

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.000
By all means.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.300
<b>Hatagaya Academy High School</b>

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.610
Hatate Souta-kun.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.000
H-Hi there.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.830
<i>A friendship flag, huh?</i>

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.420
Wh-Who might you be?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.170
My name is Mahougasawa Akane.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.210
It's Mahougasawa Akane.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.420
Maho...

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.930
So, Mahougasawa-san, right?

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.350
Akane's fine.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.600
Mahougasawa...

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.760
Akane's fine.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.180
Do you need something, Akane?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.310
It's the first time a boy's said 
my name without an honorific!

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.900
Does she have a flag?

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:53.690
Yeah.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.240
Could I eat lunch with you?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:56.860
No.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.030
He said no!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.120
Hey! You broke her flag, didn't you?

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.160
I wasn't really thinking...

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.200
I won't bug you at all, 
so we can eat together, right?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.960
You didn't break her flag?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.120
That can't be...

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.380
It's back!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.540
The flag's there again.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.250
Hm?

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.510
Can I eat with you?

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.340
No, I really don't think so.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.220
I can't?

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.300
Well, I'll just start eating until 
you really think I need to go.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.760
That's fine, right? Right?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.720
I don't know if I want to 
eat with a girl...

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.480
I can see that. I'm sorry.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.520
Sigh.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.900
Then I'll just wait until you 
finish eating, Souta-kun!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.150
Would that be all right?

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:36.900
Knock yourself out...

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.110
Yay! Great!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.450
She shattered your flag instead?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.660
Lunch, lunch! I'm so happy!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.000
Time to eat.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:47.960
Who is this girl, anyway?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.210
You don't know?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.750
You haven't heard of 
the Mahougasawa Group?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.750
She's the heir to the owner of the whole group.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.920
I see. So one of those 
super-rich girls, then.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:55.880
Not at all. Not at all.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.170
I mean Nanami-chan's a princess.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.430
She's the 13th princess of the 
Principality of Bladefield.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.970
I might be a princess,

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.940
but I'm the princess of a small 
backwater country in Europe.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.270
We've got 10 princes and

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.570
14 princesses in a small castle, 
so we don't really get along.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:19.320
That's why I got sent to this 
island nation in the first place.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.320
We're a poor principality,

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.950
so it's strange I'm 
studying overseas here.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.290
Sorry, I don't have any money...

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.700
I have lots of money.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:28.700
I don't need your money!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.710
That's right. There's something 
more important than money.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.840
It's our friendship, 
sparkling like a gem.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.550
From today forth, the three of us will

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.970
be bound by friendship, 
a bond strong than diamond.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.720
All you did is eat your lunch!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.890
That's right.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.260
So her flag comes back?

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.140
Yes,

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.520
and extremely quick at 
that. She's a toughie.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.270
I see.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.100
"Why," is the question.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:56.820
Well, she doesn't brag about being 
part of the famous Mahougasawa Group,

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.440
she's got this kind, lovable 
atmosphere about her,

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.820
and is always surrounded by friends.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.280
In short,

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.320
she has everything you don't.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.870
I don't know if that has anything 
to do with those flags you speak of.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.090
Why is someone like that 
trying to get close to me?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.010
Don't know.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.420
Try asking her.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.680
Wait up!

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.180
Hm?

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.480
Don't leave me behind!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.940
Let's all go home together.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.440
Hey...

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.690
Why are you trying to get close to me?

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.570
Well, I couldn't just leave a dog 
sitting there getting pelted by rain

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.450
or a cat pitiably crying out for help...

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.280
<i>So basically a pet?!</i>

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.660
I see.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:50.040
You're basically being charitable to 
all of the dogs and cats out there

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.870
since you have so much money.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.080
Th-That's not it...

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.920
That's not it! That's not it!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.920
I feel like you're screaming out for 
help more than any cat or dog!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.130
<i>So worse than a pet?!</i>

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:08.550
Well, given how gloom and doom you are,

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.140
you need a friend like this.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.850
Souta-kun, you'll be 
my friend, won't you?!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.400
Since we're friends,

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.480
can I go to your house, 
like friends do?!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.030
I, uh...

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.450
Oh, yeah. My house is a complete mess.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.280
Then, I'll clean!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.910
I'm a neat-freak, 
although I may not look it.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.830
Uh huh!

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.910
Do as you like.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.330
It's okay for me to like you?!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.000
Not what I meant!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.750
Cleaning!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.500
Why is this happening?!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.300
Why are you bringing me along?

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.390
You're a friend, too.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.800
We're all going together.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.560
Right. So where is this 
"Quest Dorm" place, anyway?

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.140
The station after the 
Hatsudai school station.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.480
The next station over is 
10 kilometers away, right?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.730
Hatagaya Academy is too big.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.190
I know the place is large,

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.940
but I never would have thought 
this was part of the school.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.360
A farming village?

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:07.660
We're almost there.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.790
Here we are.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.670
It's abandoned!

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.340
I told you two it was a mess.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.130
<b>Danger</b>

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.130
It's so dangerous, the sign's crooked.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.220
It's so dangerous, 
there're holes in the stairway.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.640
The holes are what make it dangerous.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:35.560
I wouldn't be surprised if the

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.350
<b>Quest Dorm</b>

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.980
floor on the second level 
collapsed at any time.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.230
This here's my room.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.400
It doesn't look much better in here.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.490
I don't have anywhere else to go.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.280
I'm just happy I have
a place to stay.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:50.660
I can't ask for much.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.200
It's the first time I've 
been to a friend's house

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.830
and been in a guy's room!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.200
That's an overstatement.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.670
You have lots of friends, don't you?

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.710
That's true...

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:02.670
Hm?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:08.470
I've wanted to be your
friend for a while now, too!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.300
Wh-Why me?!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.510
Well, I couldn't just leave a dog 
sitting there getting pelted by rain

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.760
or a cat pitiably crying out for help...

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:17.560
So I'm basically a pet, too?!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.480
It's nice to see you laugh, Souta-kun!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.070
I want you to laugh forever.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.650
I-I'm going to hit the restroom.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:34.240
I wanted to see him laugh some more.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.540
So what do you like so 
much about Souta, Akane?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.330
I have no clue.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.290
I can't stand not solving any

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:48.090
mystery that catches my eye.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.720
The first time I saw Souta-kun,

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.090
it felt like someone grabbed my heart.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:58.350
I wanted to do something for him.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.100
So love at first sight?

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.560
Love at first sight?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.610
Not that. Not at all.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.860
This story's from when I was a kid.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.910
Since I was the granddaughter of 
the head of the Mahougasawa Group,

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.160
I didn't really have any friends.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.540
They sent me to a library 
to expand my knowledge,

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.830
and that was the first time I met a 
friend my age, who felt like an equal.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.130
So exchanging the things we 
cared about was just something

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:33.130
we did to show our 
feelings for each other.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.350
But to the adults,

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.260
the things we shared had
 very different values.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.480
Our "equal" relationship was shattered,

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.150
and a wall went up that

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.900
divided us into different worlds.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.320
The Group called her

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.400
"pitiable" and looked down on her.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.790
I couldn't save her.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.830
I couldn't save that "pitiable girl."

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.540
And so I ran into Souta-kun,

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.010
and thought to myself, 
"I can save someone this time,

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.300
and if I could pull that 
off, then I could, in turn,

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:16.390
somehow make up for being 
pitiable myself so long ago."

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.890
That's why these selfish 
desires of mine aren't love.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.350
I can't let them be love.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.020
I don't really see a problem.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.110
You two are alike in a way.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:29.900
Huh?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.360
Souta said something similar.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:37.570
That people would meet misfortune if 
they got too close to him, or something.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.700
What caused you two to think like 
that may have been different,

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.250
but if you both aren't trying 
to make yourselves happy,

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:47.170
and are trying to make 
each other happy instead,

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.750
I think you both will

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.300
end up happy in the end.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.050
Nanami-chan, you're a poet!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.670
I take that back!

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.470
It was a poem! A poem!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.970
I take it all back!

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.890
It was a wonderful poem!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.890
Stop saying poem already!

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.390
Nanami, you're so wonderful!

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:05.310
What's going on here?

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.770
<b>Danger</b>

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.770
I had fun today.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.020
Can I come over again?

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:12.190
No.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.530
He said "no" again!

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.700
That's enough. Let's go home.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.910
Okay.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.160
Oh, no!

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.830
I left something in Souta-kun's room.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.080
I'm going to go get it.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.540
I guess I'll wait.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.410
Make sure you don't fall.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:33.920
That's a...

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:34.920
What's wrong?

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.260
A death flag just appeared 
above Akane's head.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.130
What?

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.340
Why isn't it breaking?

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.010
I didn't see anything that 
would bring this on...

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.180
Which means...

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:44.350
Nanami,

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.680
tell me anything you can.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.230
Do you have any idea 
what could cause this?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.850
What did you talk to Akane about?!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.730
What? You talked about her past?

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.900
What? Is that bad?

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.690
When you talk about the past,

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:59.610
it creates death flags that are 
far worse than normal ones.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.030
Damn it!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:01.820
Souta!

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.910
<i>What do I need to destroy this flag?</i>

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.330
<i>Friendship? Love? Memories?</i>

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.830
Oh, Souta-kun, I found it.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.880
Akane!

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.470
Akane!

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:23.680
Akane!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.260
Wake up, Akane!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.220
Souta-kun...

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.850
I'm sorry.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.900
I destroyed your house...

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.650
I'll call an ambulance right now.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.440
<i>The flag's getting stronger.</i>

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.110
Did that girl

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:42.820
hate me so much I fell down here?

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:43.990
No, don't be silly.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:46.200
I'm sure she wanted to be 
friends with you again.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>It's not shattering...</i>

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.790
I'm sure you're keeping that safe 
until you can see her again.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:52.750
<i>It's not shattering!</i>

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:55.000
You're going to see her again, 
and become friends with her again.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.710
<i>It's not shattering. 
Why isn't it shattering?!</i>

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.800
This happened to you because 
you weren't keeping it safe.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.010
Souta-kun,

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.350
you shouldn't be alone.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.060
You should give people hope,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.390
just like you did for me.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.400
I want you to surround yourself

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.440
by a lot more people...

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.860
and do the same for all of them.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.740
<i>No, this isn't working! 
It won't shatter!</i>

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.990
I understand...

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.240
I'll do that once you recover from this.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:28.330
<i>Wait...</i>

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.830
<i>It this a romance flag?</i>

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:30.790
<i>I see.</i>

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.120
<i>If I can't shatter that one, 
I'll just make another stand in its place!</i>

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.750
<i>A flag of life that will 
overpower the other one.</i>

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.500
Don't hate me for this, Akane.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:02.320
What are you doing?!

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:04.150
<b>Danger</b>

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:52.700
Ouch...

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:53.890
This still hurts.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:57.310
<b>Complete</b>

00:22:57.550 --> 00:22:59.910
A "conquest complete" flag, huh?

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:13.630
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.830
That was nerve-wracking,

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:18.560
but I'm sure the next episode will have 
me back to living my old, peaceful life.

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:20.600
Yeah, but you just had that flag appear.

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.290
Speaking of which, is there anyone else

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:24.240
living in the Quest Dorm with you?

00:23:23.750 --> 00:24:28.530
{commercial sPot #3}

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:28.020
Who else besides me would 
choose to live there?

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:30.070
We'll be taking one more flag.

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:31.670
It'll be just like this next time.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.590
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.950
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:34.950
<b>Girls are in the Dorm. 
But I can't say it yet. Wait until tomorrow.</b>

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.950
<b></b>
